+The generated arrays in `src/arena/beam_effects.c` contain four styles × four frames × 2,048 bytes = **32,768 tile bytes**, plus one 32-byte palette. Each frame is four contiguous 32×32 4bpp OBJ images at byte offsets 0, 512, 1024 and 1536. Each chunk contains 4×4 row-major 8×8 tiles; each byte stores the left pixel in its low nibble and the next pixel in its high nibble. This permits one selected frame per actor in a shared **2,048-byte OBJ image slot**, with four 32×32 OAM objects and one palette bank. Square chunks leave room for diagonal affine rotation.
 
 Array bounds are `style < ARENA_BEAM_STYLES` (4) and `frame < ARENA_BEAM_FRAMES` (4). Selection, animation cadence, angle, placement, and live VRAM ownership belong to the renderer; this importer only emits bounded native image and palette data.
